{"created": "2026-09-06T19:57:55.895796+00:00", "modified": "2026-09-06T19:57:56.400617+00:00", "id": 22551146, "conceptrecid": "22551145", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22551146", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.22551145", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22551146", "metadata": {"title": "A Short Resolution of Zhao's Open Problem 5.2 after the 2026 Jacobian Counterexample", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22551146", "publication_date": "2026-09-06", "description": "<p>Zhao asked in 2008 whether the Vanishing Conjecture can fail for a nonpolynomial Hessian-nilpotent formal power series over C. The 2026 failure of the Jacobian Conjecture, combined with Zhao's 2007 equivalence, supplies a homogeneous quartic Hessian-nilpotent polynomial P0 for which the Vanishing Conjecture fails. We adjoin two fresh variables and a nonpolynomial isotropic tail R=q(u+iv). Zhao's own disjoint-sum identity then gives exact additivity of Delta^m P^(m+1), while every power of R is harmonic. Hence P0+R is a nonpolynomial Hessian-nilpotent formal power series for which the Vanishing Conjecture fails. This closes Open Problem 5.2. The mechanism is principally a post-2026 corollary of Zhao's published machinery; priority is not claimed.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Atwell, Casey", "affiliation": null}], "keywords": ["Hessian nilpotent polynomials", "formal power series", "Vanishing Conjecture", "Jacobian conjecture", "Zhao Open Problem 5.2", "Laplacian", "disjoint formal power series"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.1090/S0002-9947-06-03898-0", "relation": "cites", "resource_type": "publication-article", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.4064/ap93-2-3", "relation": "cites", "resource_type": "publication-article", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.21554281", "relation": "cites", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "https://isa-afp.org/entries/Jacobian_Counterexample.html", "relation": "cites", "resource_type": "software", "scheme": "url"}], "version": "1.0.0", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "22551145"}}]}}, "title": "A Short Resolution of Zhao's Open Problem 5.2 after the 2026 Jacobian Counterexample", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22551146", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22551146", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22551146?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22551146", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22551146", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.22551146", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22551146/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22551145", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22551145", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22551145", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.22551145", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22551146/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22551146/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22551146/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22551146/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22551146:01_Atwell_Zhao_OP5_2_v1.0.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22551146:01_Atwell_Zhao_OP5_2_v1.0.pdf/full/%5E50,/0/default.jpg", "100": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22551146:01_Atwell_Zhao_OP5_2_v1.0.pdf/full/%5E100,/0/default.jpg", "250": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22551146:01_Atwell_Zhao_OP5_2_v1.0.pdf/full/%5E250,/0/default.jpg", "750": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22551146:01_Atwell_Zhao_OP5_2_v1.0.pdf/full/%5E750,/0/default.jpg", "1200": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22551146:01_Atwell_Zhao_OP5_2_v1.0.pdf/full/%5E1200,/0/de